      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s certainly possible! What are your thoughts there?\n\nThe issue with chromium is that there\u0027s not central place for it. We\u0027ll theoretically need this in services/viz, gpu/ cc/ and blink/ and there already multiple places where there\u0027s some kind of \"skia_utils\" file. One of the ideas for this project is to de-dupe a lot of stuff and just couple with skia more directly (see platform/graphics/color.h and crbug.com/1167153).\n\nAlso, having it on the class means that we can have stuff like:\ncolor1.approximatelyEquals(color2, epsilon);\n\nWhereas with a helper function we\u0027d need a separate import (with potential namespacing weirdness) and:\nSkColor4fApproximatelyEquals(color1, color2, epsilon);\n\nI\u0027d also be worried if I stashed this in chromium somewhere that another dev some day adds another function that works slightly differently in a different place. What\u0027s the reason to keep it off of SkColor?",
